## Monitoring & Observability

### Metrics to Track
```
TelegramRouter level:
  - Requests per minute
  - Requests by endpoint
  - Average latency
  - Error rate

LeaderBotManager level:
  - Active leader bots
  - Bot spawn success rate
  - Bot idle time distribution
  - Memory per bot

UserSession level:
  - Active sessions per user
  - Tasks completed per user
  - Total blocks placed per user
  - Build success rate
```

### Alerts to Set Up
```
WARNING:
  - Bot spawn takes >30 seconds
  - Bot memory >500MB
  - Error rate >1%
  - Response latency >5 seconds

CRITICAL:
  - More than 5 consecutive spawn failures
  - Memory usage >90% of available
  - Crash/restart loop detected
  - Webhook delivery failures
```

---

## Conclusion

**Per-User Leader Bot Architecture is ideal for:**
- Multi-user Telegram bot systems
- Parallel builds and workflows
- Scalable to 50+ concurrent users
- Complete resource and session isolation
- Independent fault domains

**Compared to alternatives:**
- Better than single bot (no blocking)
- Better than queuing (no artificial delay)
- Better than threads (Minecraft.js not thread-safe)
- Better than stateless (maintains per-user state)

**Investment required:**
- 3-4 new source files (~600 lines)
- SQLite database (~2KB)
- Additional ~15GB memory for 50 users
- Moderate operational complexity

**Returns:**
- 10x better user experience
- True horizontal scalability
- Complete session isolation
- Built-in fault tolerance
